f('child-hymn-promises','SUPPORTED','25.56–61',evs(['child-hymn-promises-kumaras-return'])+refs('boons_and_powers',['mud6-power-kumaras-child-hymn-benefits','mud6-power-kumaras-ganapatya-promise'],['recipient_id','grantor_id','requested','granted','trigger','notes']),'Child’s reader/hearer benefits and Gaṇapatya promise go to the proper recipients.','57–58 explicitly grant yoga-peace/desired benefits via the hymn and tell the Kumāras they will be Gaṇapatyas like Śiva. No additional personal request is quoted. The child resumes ordinary-looking play; the Kumāras visit the king, receive hospitality and return. These are not a new Pṛthu-directed apparition/grant.')
f('prthu-wife-final-merger','SUPPORTED','25.62–64',evs(['prthu-wife-final-merger'])+rels(['prthu-sons-group','prthu-kingdom-division','prwife-ganesa-merger'])+refs('boons_and_powers',['mud6-power-prthu-account-benefits'],['trigger','granted']),'Plural unnamed sons receive divided rule; forest practice ends in actual joint merger with wife.','62 gives the Kumāras’ return to Brahmā’s world and Pṛthu’s kingdom division among sons;63 gives progressive yoga/Gaṇapatya state and actual end-merger with wife in Gaṇeśa. No wife name, specific son list or mere prospective substitute is introduced.64 hearing/reading benefits are separate. This bounded ending check does not independently certify every philosophical field in25.1–43.')
