md='# Independent Mudgala review: Dhruva and Pṛthu\n\nWhole2.23.1–34 and2.24.1–54 were independently read through colophons. Bounded2.25.44–64 and2.26.1–5/42–45 were compared; this is not exhaustive whole26 review. [Primary Sanskrit witness]('+U+').\n\nThe family, teacher/mantra counts, Viṣṇu grant versus relay conditions and actual endings are supported. Pṛthu/unnamed wife emerge from Vena’s right aṅga; Earth is adopted daughter, and all calf/milker/product assignments are supported. Six Indra horse thefts and ninety-nine actual sacrifices are explicit; reconciliation spares Indra. The child’s hymn promises belong to the Kumāras/readers, while Pṛthu/wife actually merge later. Prācīnabarhis’s final kingdom handoff is to ministers.\n\nThe one required correction is already proposed centrally: mud6-power-dhruva-visnu-grant.duration must be null, with the thousand-year tapas preserved in austerity_or_circumstances.2.23.9 describes practice before Viṣṇu appears, not the duration of the granted kingship or abode. I support root_boon_duration_finding.json exactly.\n\n2.23.29 direction and31 varṣamāsaṃ residence remain UNDETERMINED; keep chapter/story PARTIAL and raw Sanskrit. No modern location or normalized year/month period is supplied.\n\nFindings: '+str(r['status_counts'])+'. Distinct checked IDs: '+str(r['total_distinct_record_ids'])+' ('+', '.join(f'{len(v)} {k}' for k,v in ids.items())+'). Detailed JSON lists exact affected fields and checked clauses.\n\nFrozen target SHA-256: '+sha+'. No patch/output files edited. Independent print/expert collation remains separate.\n'
